course: dictionary
lesson: 11910
title: Burdened: carrying a load
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Burdened» means carrying a heavy load, or feeling weighed down by something hard to carry. «The hiker was burdened with a heavy pack all the way up the mountain.» The pack is a real weight on his back.
explain: «Mia felt burdened by her worries about the test.» Her worries are not a real object, but they feel heavy, like a load. The word can describe a real weight or a heavy feeling.
explain: Look for clue words that come with burdened, such as burdened with, burdened by or heavily burdened. To check your meaning, swap in weighed down. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Burdened means carrying a heavy load, or weighed down by worries, duties, debts or problems.
fact: Burdened is often followed by with or by, as in «burdened with debt» or «burdened by worries».
fact: «Heavily burdened» means weighed down very much.
fact: «Burdened» is also the past tense of «burden», as in «The rain burdened the old roof with water.»
fact: A burden is a heavy load, and it can be a load you carry in your head as well as on your back.
exercise: «The donkey was burdened with heavy sacks of grain.» What does burdened mean here? | Feeling very happy | *Carrying a heavy load | Running very fast | Lost on the road
exercise: «The family was burdened by debt after the shop closed.» What were they weighed down by? | *Money they owed | Sunny weather | Kind neighbours | A long holiday
exercise: Which word means weighed down by problems or worries? | Cheerful | Speedy | *Burdened | Bright
test: «Tom felt burdened by his worries about school.» What does burdened mean here? | Covered in paint | Very excited | Fast asleep | *Weighed down by worries
test: «The old king was heavily burdened with duties.» What does heavily burdened mean? | Light as a feather | *Weighed down very much by duties | Happily dancing | Ready for a party
exam: «The farmer was burdened with debts and worries.» What does burdened mean here? | Playing outside | Dancing at a party | *Weighed down by money problems and worries | Cooking a meal
